  "reviews": [
    {
      "author": "MovieGuys",
      "content": "\"Murderer Report\" is not what it first seems. \r\n\r\nThis is a very layered crime thriller, where assumptions about the motivations and underlying morality, of a serial killer, being interviewed, by a reporter, increasingly challenge both mordern societal and fundamental human norms, raising questions about what it means to psychologically \"cured\", to be made whole again, as the story gradually, unfolds. \r\n\r\nIts a engaging premise, where detailed characteristions, with complex, fluid perspectives, drive this film to its disturbing but nonetheless, satisfying conclusion.\r\n\r\nIn summary, a compelling story, complex characterisations, with wholly plausible motivations, married up with great acting. If you like crime thrillers, this is a must watch.",
      "rating": 8,
      "createdAt": "2025-12-20T20:53:06Z"
    },
    {
      "author": "Alunauwie",
      "content": "Murderer Report unfolds as a restrained psychological duel, where quiet conversations slowly blur the line between empathy and moral justification. Through manipulative dialogue and minimalistic staging, the film builds suffocating tension without relying on spectacle. Its predictable yet deliberate ending reinforces a lingering question about justice, guilt, and how society often pressures victims to simply move on.\r\n\r\nRead the full review here: (Indonesian version : alunauwie.com) and  (English version : uwiepuspita.com)",
      "rating": 8,
      "createdAt": "2026-01-31T04:25:35Z"
    }
  ],
